      "description": "The info-metric pattern: model_info is a gauge that is always 1, and its LABELS are the payload. This is link ten of the course's traceability chain — the dashboard can name the model behind every other panel, so a latency step change can be attributed to a deployment without leaving the browser. Note what would have gone wrong if model_version had been a label on http_requests_total instead: a deploy would look like a traffic drop, because the old series stops and a new one starts at zero.",
